From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 09:53:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: add i386 userspace task support

Add the complete i386 process ABI to the dedicated x86-family UML slice: ELF loading, task and register mode, signal frames, TLS, ptrace register layout, restart handling, and compat structure translation.

Generate the i386 dispatch table from the canonical Linux 6.18 syscall specification, retaining slice-owned adapters where x86 ABI layouts or argument order differ, and dispatch long-mode INT 0x80 through it. Keep this isolated from normal arm64 and Android configurations.
